    <bpmn:process id="W_W4168" name="W4168. PIM/DAM Platform, Integration &amp; Lifecycle Governance" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Platform review; upgrade; integration change; lifecycle governance
Frequency: Annual + on change
Volume: Enterprise PIM/DAM platform serving 6 channels + B2B
Owner: PIM Product Owner / Enterprise Architecture (VS-113) / IT (VS-27)
Participants: IT (VS-27), EA (VS-113), Ecommerce (VS-10), TBM/FinOps (VS-135), InfoSec (VS-27.3)
Source: workflow W4168 — PIM/DAM Platform, Integration &amp; Lifecycle Governance</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W4168_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W4168_Lane1" name="PIM Owner">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4168_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4168_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4168_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4168_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4168_End7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W4168_Start3" name="Platform review; upgrade; integration change; lifecycle governance">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4168_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4168_Task4" name="PIM/EA/IT govern the PIM/DAM platform lifecycle — roadmap, upgrades, vendor…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: PIM/EA/IT govern the PIM/DAM platform lifecycle — roadmap, upgrades, vendor management, scalability (35K→growth, asset volume), and cost (links to VS-135 TBM)
Responsible (R): PIM Owner / EA / IT
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: Annual</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4168_Flow10</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4168_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4168_Task5" name="PIM/EA govern integration architecture (ERP item master VS-29, ecommerce VS-10…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: PIM/EA govern integration architecture (ERP item master VS-29, ecommerce VS-10, marketplace VS-65, retail-media VS-48, print, CDP VS-126) via the integration layer (VS-113.2) with versioning/monitoring
Responsible (R): PIM Owner / EA
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: Continuous</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4168_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4168_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4168_Task6" name="PIM/InfoSec govern platform security (access control, vendor portal VS-27.3…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: PIM/InfoSec govern platform security (access control, vendor portal VS-27.3, data privacy of customer-linked content VS-91), and conduct periodic DR/BCP testing (VS-26) for the content platform
Responsible (R): PIM Owner / InfoSec
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: Annual</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4168_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4168_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W4168_End7" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W4168_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W4168_Annotation8">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-149 (ensure product content accuracy &amp; rights compliance.) | - CTL-643: platform lifecycle governed (VS-113); DR/BCP tested (VS-26); security/privacy assessed (VS-27.3/VS-91)
Owner: PIM Product Owner / Enterprise Architecture (VS-113) / IT (VS-27)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
